WEBVTT

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.210
The following tale is a work of pure fiction.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.760
<b> January 1st 1582</b>

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.760
<b> Omi Province Azuchi</b>

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:54.150
This new hall, "Imperial Veneration," shall serve to welcome the Emperor,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.240
should we be graced by his presence. {miyuki no ma ni gozaimasu}

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.250
'Tis disastrous...

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.450
An Imperial visit signifies the Emperor's weakening grasp of power {until koto wa}

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:16.460
and the acknowledgment of Milord's vast influence.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.960
Should I fail to achieve great feats, becoming a Lord shall be beyond my grasp.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:28.100
At present, there are too few feats to be achieved.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.110
Though this junction be disastrous... {until ichimai}

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:39.740
might I leave with one screen?

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.740
<b>Topple Takeda</b>

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:43.850
Forward! {tsugi}

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.130
Forward! {tsugi}

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:48.750
Forward!

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:54.840
Forward!

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.960
Milord collects the offerings?

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.870
'Tis dreadful to grant audience to every single offering personally in my quarters.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.010
Now, 100 mon

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.220
to welcome the New Year.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.370
My offerings to the New-

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.610
Forward!

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.860
Delayed were you, Governor Furuta?

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.500
Long has it been,

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.240
General Hosokawa Tadaoki.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:32.140
Do forgive my absence at your wedding to General Akechi's daughter, Lady Tama.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.250
Return ye to the Yamashiro Province?

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.110
Nay,

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:38.690
I shall depart for our forces encampment in Mino.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.210
We are to attack Takeda's remaining forces soon.

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.380
Won't you visit my residence?

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.580
Though a mere trifle to others, I've obtained a lovely Ming flower vase.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.450
The price of such beauty comes to 120 koku,

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.170
and I wished to share it with others.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.090
He may afford such leisure with his achievements.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:06.630
In his youth, together with his father, General Hosokawa Fujitaka, both were awarded control over the vast Tango Province.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.910
And yet, my achievements pale so...

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:14.560
Sour not the mood of the New Years festivities with brood.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.150
A pleasant New Years to you both.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.860
Greetings, Master Soueki.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.070
I eagerly yearn to learn more of tea brewery from ye, Master.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:28.420
I have many to visit, and inquire of their tidings for the New Year.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:31.110
Tell me, when may I meet with your father?

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:34.810
I believe he shall be available following his three-day ceremony with poets.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.840
Do enjoy the first day of the New Year.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.750
Master Soueki shall occupy himself for quite a while.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.180
The fence has collapsed!

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.130
Those waiting to relinquish their offerings rest against the fence,

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.240
but it failed to support the weight of so many! {omosa ni taikirenakattarashii}

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.880
<b> January 1582</b>

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.880
<b> Tango Province Miyazu Castle {ts}</b>

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:06.970
General Hosokawa, 'tis a most splendid Ming flower vase.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.680
'Twas a gift from Tadaoki.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:16.210
Though he is a valiant warrior, he devotes his heart to tea brewery as of late.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.840
Do forgive my crude words, Tea Master.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:24.410
However, there is naught to gain through obsession.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:29.520
A warrior should know the essence of art, but never pledge devotion to it. {until okubeki}

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:35.200
Even with essence, the men of our age know naught of the old classics.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.390
Nay, they sing blind praises for our own brand of ceramics.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:45.360
I believe those who forsake history and the old classics may achieve little as warriors.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.780
Do you not agree?

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:57.000
True are your words.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:01.880
Master Soueki knows much of the old classics.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:08.410
With wisdom of both tea and old classics, may ye polish my son further.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.660
Woe, were he led astray by harmful philosophies. {go kyoujuu nasaranu you ni}

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:18.400
Regarding to the men of our age, I've heard of naught but their disloyalty

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.170
as of late.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.540
Such as?

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:31.800
They glorify Araki Murashige and Matsunaga Hisahide, and regard them as heroes.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:40.110
Supposedly, both rebels harbored the same ambition to usurp Milord {until gegokujou wo nashitoge}

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:43.860
before Milord may achieve unification.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:52.370
Glorify as they will, both rebels were naught but insects before Milord's ambition.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.440
Such men are peasants, who know naught of being a true warrior.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.850
Dare such peasants forsake their gratitude to their Lord?

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:06.950
'Tis natural for men to serve one whose vast power ensures their own survival. {until ikinokoru sube}

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.740
Are ye not one of such men? {until fujitakasama tote}

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:20.820
Were such men to rise and grasp power, they would remain as rebels.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:25.040
History and the old classics have taught us the fate of all rebels.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.730
Therefore, I am not one of such cowardly men.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.240
Devotion, claim ye?

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.760
Indeed.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.250
Tadaoki would claim absolute devotion as I.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:40.640
Our devout warriors of the Tango Province would dare serve no rebel.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:47.250
The merchants of Sakai, myself included, owe a great deal to Milord.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:56.780
Were one to rebel against Milord, Sakai merchants would henceforth cease assistance to such a rebel.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.930
And we do so to ensure our own survival.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:05.380
May I interpret that as a warning?

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:11.360
'Tis merely the concerns a weary aesthete.

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:15.030
You have my gratitude for the tea.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:18.670
Do forgive me for my childish fervor.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:20.660
Won't you stay for the night?

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:24.500
Nay, as I have others to visit and inquire of their tidings for the New Year.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.040
'Tis most earnest of ye.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.650
Where do you travel to now?

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:34.470
I shall visit General Akechi's vassal, General Tsutsui Junkei.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.950
<b> January 1582</b>

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:37.950
<b> Mino Province Yamaguchi Castle {ts}</b>

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.930
'Twas in that castle which Governor Furuta was reared as a child?

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:43.380
Aye.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.230
The Furuta clan were independent from other clans.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:49.510
Though, during my childhood, we had served the ruling Toki clan of Mino.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:51.460
'Twas a pleasant time...

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:55.480
I had often enjoyed ripened persimmons.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:09:00.140
'Twas Autumn when both the fields and setting sun appeared as a ripe persimmon. {until majiwatte mou}

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.520
Overwhelming, was the beauty of such a sight.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.690
Greetings, Governor Furuta!

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:10.420
Long has it been, Master Katou Kagenobu.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:15.740
You have my sincerest gratitude for the beautiful Shino tea bowl.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.830
Use these materials for your craft.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.930
You have my gratitude.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:26.080
The Great Kiln is occupied with many orders, aye?

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:31.260
Though Milord requests the craft of many simple wares,

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.530
I have yet to craft one to be considered decent.

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:34.690
How unfortunate...

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:37.490
I have tried many forms, without success.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:40.900
Though, my Shino wares bake to perfection in the Muta Cave Kiln.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:42.700
How peculiar...

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:47.230
'Tis a relic, dug up around these parts recently.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:51.150
Though I've beheld this object once in Kamikuze,

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.360
I long for this protruded pattern, for it intrigues me so.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:57.030
Would you like to see the kiln?

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.680
I've replaced the older kiln with a larger one,

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.190
so that I may bake even more simple wares.

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:13.710
Master Kagenobu, beheld ye the Ido tea bowl of the Joseon Kingdom?

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.630
I've beheld the one in Milord's possession many a time.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:21.570
The most notable and difficult to achieve quality of that masterpiece is the loquatesque hue. {until muzukashu gozaru}

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.290
Won't... {hitotsu}

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:29.190
you bake an Ido tea bowl for me?

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.290
Aye... {hou}

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:34.820
It need not be identical to Milord's Ido tea bowl, mind you.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:39.510
However, the craft may not be to your liking...

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.610
It shall suffice.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.260
<b> February 1582</b>

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.260
<b> Shinano Province Ojima Castle {ts}</b>

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.400
We shall press the assault on Takeda's remaining territories!

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:58.430
When the deaths of Takeda Katsuyori and his retainers are achieved,

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:02.410
then, may I welcome Father to his new territories of Kai and Shinano!

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.780
General Tokugawa Ieyasu sieges Katsuyori's castle from Suruga,

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.200
while assisted by General Hojo Ujimasa from Kanto.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:12.170
My uncle, Oda Nagamasa, shall approach from Kiso and lay siege to Fukashi Castle.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:15.930
Though Nishina Morinobu, Katsuyori's little brother, defends Takatou Castle,

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:18.930
he remains the most formidable of foes.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:22.590
The small fortress of Fukuyou Castle bordering Takatou Castle must be captured with minimal effort. {until otoshitai}

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.800
Be there a warrior to accept this task?

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.060
I shall accept this task.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:33.210
Our forces shall leave for Takatou Castle in two days.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:36.940
Regardless of the scale, the reward for capturing the castle shall be grand!

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.990
Are you certain of this venture?

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:45.220
Was it not I who had convinced a warrior such as yourself to serve Milord?

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.200
Woe, for this war may be...

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:56.700
the last opportunity I have to garner achievements.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.300
Should I relinquish this opportunity, {kore wo nogaseba}

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:02.720
my life shall end not as a Lord, but as a common Governor.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:07.970
The simple wares of Master Katou Kagenobu

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.980
shall be my most trusted allies for the battles to come.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:16.160
Milord calls for your submission.

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:21.200
His son, Lord Nobutada, shall arrive with a force 50,000 to capture this castle.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:24.240
Should ye surrender, Lord Nobutada shall be lenient with you.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:29.220
Was it not this son who ordered the execution of Araki Murashige's surviving clan members?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.740
His "lenience" is akin to death.

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:34.890
Death unto your clan shall be the result of your refusal to Milord's lenience.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.340
Our loyalty shan't waver.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:57.860
Though we are foes alike, I've naught but compassion for devoted warriors.

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:03.000
Milord has bestowed upon ye a masterpiece even he is hesitant to part with. {until tazusaeteita}

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.880
This Ido tea bowl of the Joseon Kingdom

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:08.280
is known as "Thick Persimmon." {mei wo boudangaki}

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:11.670
Take this bowl and withdraw from the castle.

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:13.770
With this one bowl,

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:17.000
your clan shall be ensured 50 years of food. {issho tabete yukaremasuzo}

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:31.790
This is an Ido tea bowl?!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.900
I've heard of its marvelous figure,

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:35.600
but this appears rather crude. {sukoshi misuborashikunaika}

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:39.770
Have ye any means to authenticate this bowl?!

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.280
None. {kekkou de gozaru}

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:52.450
As it stands, ye have refused my goodwill.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:55.120
Now, your clan shall be ensured execution. {mohaya nan no tedasuke mo dekimasen}

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:58.110
Farewell.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.130
Just a moment! {matare}

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.640
General!

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:17.810
Due to my stratagem, the Lord of Fukuyou Castle and his retainers

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:21.950
have fled the castle, and is now occupied by our forces!

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:23.360
Ye have done well!

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.170
I shall inform my father of your feats!

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:29.760
Well done, indeed.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.930
How did you persuade them?

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:35.090
With naught but a hook before a starving fish.

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:39.940
Though, the loss of a such a lovely hook stings my heart.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:46.550
<b> March 1582</b>

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:46.550
<b> Shinano Province Takatou Castle {ts}</b>

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:55.440
Nishina Morinobu too formidable a foe.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:01.440
Though we've dispatched the second messenger, his forces morale has yet to deplete.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:06.830
General Tokugawa has succeeded in persuading General Anayama Baisetsu to our side.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:09.890
We must hasten our capture of Takatou and assist General Tokugawa's assault on Katsuyori's castle!

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.090
Milord!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:17.720
Lord Oda Nagamasu has successfully taken Fukashi Castle!

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:18.730
What?! {nani}

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:21.460
He has?!

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:27.150
Very well!

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:29.610
We shall assault Takatou Castle at dawn!

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.720
Just a moment, General!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.620
Allow me the opportunity to persuade them once more!

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:42.830
Ye shan't succeed.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.840
Nishina Morinobu is the proud fifth son of Takeda Shingen.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.070
He shan't be persuaded by a mere messenger.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.580
Then go, now!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.910
Be wary that our assault begins at dawn.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:06.750
Aye? {yoi na}

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:10.060
Aye. {ha}

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:16.230
The venerable monk was sent as a messenger...

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:17.850
His nose is gone... {nante koto shiyagaru}

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.890
Forsake not morale,

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.150
for my ascension above Lord Nagamasa shall be delayed!

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:34.640
I shall...

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:40.550
succeed as a warrior, to avenge my defeat to that aesthete! {until bu de kaesu}{second semete stuck in this line}

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:43.180
My heart shan't falter!

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:54.320
Milord resides in the keep.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:00.200
Messenger, know this.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:05.500
We welcome death.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:11.390
Should you fail here, the next messenger shall lose his nose as well.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.070
They shall serve as our final meal before death.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.390
Welcome death, do ye?

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:34.670
I've heard naught but the exact same from the men of defeated Lords. {until tsumaranu serifu yo}

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:42.320
To me, parting with one's own life is a simple, yet difficult task.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:46.060
However, parting with treasure is the most difficult.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:48.400
Identify yourself!

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:53.390
I am Furuta Sasuke, messenger of Milord Oda Nobunaga.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:56.700
I wish to meet with your lord, Nishina Morinobu.

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.700
Milord is meditating at present!

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:01.380
None shall disturb Milord's meditation!

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:05.700
Know ye of the tea scoop?

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:09.730
'Tis a grand masterpiece crafted by Master Shutoku.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:14.300
I wished to bequeath this unto your lord,

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.870
but I have many others to bequeath.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:19.800
I advise ye leave the castle with this masterpiece.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:24.680
'Twill sustain you for a lifetime.

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:27.390
I've no need for wood scrap!

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:32.030
This accursed child discards a scoop of my own craft?!

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:35.930
Then does this interest you?

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:40.950
'Tis the "Excreted Persimmon" incense pot of the Joseon Kingdom.

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:43.260
"Excreted Persimmon?!"

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:48.490
Long ago, a Joseon potter unintentionally dropped this very bowl into a pond of waste.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:54.110
To repent on his own foolishness, he then baked and glazed it as it was. {until yaita tokoro}

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:59.590
The result was this glowing, yet beautiful masterpiece that even the potter was said to be most fond of.

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:08.810
Though, perhaps this masterpiece fails to tingle the fascination of youths.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:11.730
Do forgive me for my ramblings-

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:20.720
'Tis the obvious reaction to Master Kagenobu's craft.

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:24.570
It's beauty carries even the weight of a false account.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:27.890
Perhaps such beauty was wasted upon that foolish child...

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:35.650
Identify yourself!

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.510
Harm not an Ido bowl of Joseon!

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:45.140
'Tis meant for General Nishina Morinobu as a term of surrender!

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:57.250
This is no Ido tea bowl.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:04.990
Both the essential shagreen base and imprinting are absent.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:06.620
Curses! {mazui}

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.560
She possesses a discerning eye!

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:20.960
Ye are steadfast and impudent to dare another negotiation.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:25.550
Copulate with me, and I shall pardon your impudence.

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:32.480
I know that death shall come unto the Takeda clan momentarily.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.280
I would fulfill my loyalty to Milord in death...

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:40.330
but this need not be said.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:46.200
Now, grant unto me pleasure!

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:54.840
Very well.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.780
With the hands of a fulfilled aesthete,

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:03.740
I shall grant unto thee a night of passion.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:08.990
We shall lay siege to Takatou Castle!

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.100
Take the heads of Nishina Morinobu and his kin!

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:18.380
Return to me unharmed, Sasuke.

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:26.990
I am incapable of copulating any further.

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:33.760
You have my gratitude.

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:38.730
Where do you go?

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:46.480
I shan't face death contently now!

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:50.090
I shall wander the lands in search of a true warrior!

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:55.100
Parting with one's life is quite difficult.

00:21:55.830 --> 00:22:00.630
In the face of death, the lust of a woman is most formidable.

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:16.080
My achievements and future awaits above these stairs!

00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:31.220
I shall persuade Nishina to surrender,

00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:37.660
and as my fame spreads across the land,

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:41.020
I shall become a true Lord!

00:24:36.070 --> 00:24:37.630
<b> Truly, hilarious a man ye be {ts}</b>

00:24:42.710 --> 00:24:44.380
<b> I was not aware{ts}</b>

00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:51.100
<b> Very well! {ts}</b>

